/**
 * @fn std::string SageInterface::getMangledNameFromCache(SgNode* astNode)
 *
 * @brief Retrieves a mangled name from a cache based on an Abstract Syntax Tree (AST) node.
 *
 * This function attempts to retrieve a precomputed mangled name for the given AST node
 * from a cache. The cache is stored in a map that associates AST nodes with their corresponding
 * mangled names. If the mangled name is found in the cache, it is returned immediately;
 * otherwise, an empty string is returned.
 *
 * @param astNode The Abstract Syntax Tree (AST) node for which to retrieve the mangled name.
 *                Must be a valid pointer to an SgNode object.
 *
 * @return The precomputed mangled name associated with the given AST node if found in the cache;
 *         otherwise, an empty string is returned.
 *
 * @warning This function does not perform any error checking on the input astNode parameter.
 *          It assumes that the caller has already validated the pointer.
 *
 * @pre The global scope of the AST node must be accessible to retrieve the mangled name cache.
 *
 * @post If the mangled name is found in the cache, it is returned; otherwise, an empty string is returned.
 *
 * @note This function uses a recursive approach to find the global scope if it cannot be determined
 *       from the input AST node directly. It traverses up the AST hierarchy until it finds a valid
 *       global scope or reaches the root of the tree.
 *
 * @example This example demonstrates how to use this function:
 *          @code
 *           SgNode* astNode = ...; // assume some valid AST node
 *           std::string mangledName = SageInterface::getMangledNameFromCache(astNode);
 *           if (!mangledName.empty()) {
 *               printf("Mangled name found: %s\n", mangledName.c_str());
 *           } else {
 *               printf("Mangled name not found in cache.\n");
 *           }
 *          @endcode
 */
/**
 * @fn std::string SageInterface::addMangledNameToCache( SgNode* astNode, const std::string & oldMangledName)
 *
 * @brief Adds a mangled name to the cache for a given node in the Abstract Syntax Tree (AST).
 *
 * This function is used to update the mangled name cache with a new or modified mangled name
 * for a specific node in the AST. It takes into account whether short names are being used and
 * performs necessary transformations, such as hashing or substring coding, if needed.
 * The updated mangled name is then stored in the cache for future reference.
 *
 * @param astNode The node in the Abstract Syntax Tree (AST) for which to update the mangled name.
 * @param oldMangledName The original mangled name associated with the given AST node.
 * @return The updated mangled name after applying transformations, if any.
 */

/** 
 * @details This function performs the following steps:
