/**
 * @fn void SageInterface::setBaseTypeDefiningDeclaration(SgVariableDeclaration* var_decl, SgDeclarationStatement* base_decl)
 *
 * @brief Sets the base type defining declaration for a variable declaration.
 *
 * This function sets the base type defining declaration for a given variable
 * declaration. It first checks if the base declaration statement is already in
 * the scope's declaration list and removes it if necessary. Then, it sets the
 * parent of the base declaration to the variable declaration and updates the
 * internal mangled name.
 *
 * The function also handles comments associated with the base declaration
 * by moving them to the variable declaration to avoid potential problems.
 *
 * @param var_decl The variable declaration for which the base type defining declaration is to be set.
 *                 Must not be null.
 * @param base_decl The base declaration statement that defines the base type of the variable declaration.
 *                  Must not be null.
 *
 * @return None
 *
 * @warning If the base declaration has a comment and it is the first statement in its scope,
 *          moving comments to the variable declaration may cause unexpected behavior.
 *
 * @pre var_decl and base_decl must not be null.
 * @post The base type defining declaration for var_decl is set to base_decl, and the internal
 *       mangled name is updated if necessary.
 *
 * @note This function modifies the AST by removing the base declaration from its scope's
 *       declaration list and updating the parent of the base declaration.
 *
 * @example This example demonstrates how to use this function:
 *          @code
 *           SgVariableDeclaration* var_decl = ...;
 *           SgDeclarationStatement* base_decl = ...;
 *           SageInterface::setBaseTypeDefiningDeclaration(var_decl, base_decl);
 *          @endcode
 */
/**
 * @fn bool SageInterface::declarationPreceedsDefinition(SgDeclarationStatement* nonDefiningDeclaration, SgDeclarationStatement* definingDeclaration)
 *
 * @brief Determines if a non-defining declaration precedes the corresponding defining declaration in the AST.
 *
 * This function checks whether a given non-defining declaration appears before its
 * corresponding defining declaration in the Abstract Syntax Tree (AST). It uses a preorder
 * traversal to test the order of declaration. If the non-defining and defining declarations are
 * identical, it returns false by default.
 *
 * @param nonDefiningDeclaration The non-defining declaration statement.
 * @param definingDeclaration The defining declaration statement.
 *
 * @return True if the non-defining declaration precedes the defining declaration in the AST,
 *         false otherwise. If the input declarations are not found during traversal, it returns true
 *         to avoid incorrect assumptions about their order.
 *
 * @warning This function may return incorrect results if the input declarations are not found
 *          during traversal or if there are hidden island problems.
 *
 * @pre The input nonDefiningDeclaration and definingDeclaration must be valid SgDeclarationStatement objects.
 * @post The function will return a boolean value indicating whether the non-defining declaration precedes the defining declaration.
 */
