/**
 * @fn void SageInterface::prependStatement(SgStatement* stmt, SgScopeStatement* scope)
 *
 * @brief Prepends a statement to the beginning of a given scope.
 *
 * This function inserts a given statement at the beginning of a specified scope. 
 * It first checks if the input statement and scope are valid. If either is NULL, 
 * it uses the top scope from the SageBuilder's stack or asserts an error. 
 * Then it fixes the statement by resetting internal maps for the target statement 
 * and its associated macro expansions. Finally, it prepends the fixed statement 
 * to the beginning of the given scope.
 *
 * @param stmt The statement to be prepended to the scope. Must not be NULL.
 * @param scope The scope into which the statement is to be inserted. If NULL, 
 *              uses the top scope from SageBuilder's stack.
 *
 * @return None
 *
 * @warning This function does not handle side effects like appendStatement() does.
 *
 * @pre stmt != NULL, or it will assert an error.
 * @post The statement has been successfully prepended to the beginning of the given scope.
 *
 * @note If this is a moved statement, internal data structures are updated to record 
 *       it being moved and associated macro expansions are marked as transformations.
 *
 * @example This example demonstrates how to use this function:
 *          @code
 *              SgStatement* stmt = ...; // some statement
 *              SgScopeStatement* scope = ...; // some scope
 *              SageInterface::prependStatement(stmt, scope);
 *          @endcode
 */
