 *      The input SgScopeStatement pointer scope is not null and has a valid scope.
 *
 * @post The input scope statement has been modified to include all statements from the input vector stmts,
 *       in reverse order, at its beginning. The original statements within the scope remain unchanged.
 *
 * @note This function does not perform any checks on the validity of the input statements or their compatibility
 *       with the target scope statement. It is the caller's responsibility to ensure that the input data is correct.
 *
 * @example This example demonstrates how to use this function:
 *          @code
 *           SgScopeStatement* myScope = ...; // some valid scope statement
 *           std::vector<SgStatement*> stmtList;
 *           stmtList.push_back(new SgVariableDeclaration(...)); // add statements to the list
 *           SageInterface sageInterface;
 *           sageInterface.prependStatementList(stmtList, myScope);
 *          @endcode
 */
/**
