 * @brief Inserts a new statement before or after a target statement in an AST.
 *
 * This function recursively traverses the AST to find the parent of the target statement,
 * then inserts the new statement either before or after the target statement, depending on
 * the value of the insertBefore parameter. It also updates the links between nodes in the AST
 * if necessary.
 *
 * @param scope The current scope in which the insertion is taking place.
 * @param targetStmt The target statement where the new statement will be inserted.
 * @param newStmt The new statement to be inserted.
 * @param insertBefore A flag indicating whether to insert the new statement before or after the target statement.
 */

/**
 * @fn void SageInterface::insertStatementList(SgStatement* targetStmt, const std::vector<SgStatement*>& newStmts, bool insertBefore)
 *
 * @brief Inserts a list of statements before or after a target statement in the AST.
 *
 * This function inserts a vector of SgStatement objects into the Abstract Syntax Tree (AST) at the position specified by the target statement and the insertBefore flag. 
 * If insertBefore is true, the new statements are inserted before the target statement; otherwise, they are inserted after it.
 *
 * @param targetStmt The statement in the AST where the new statements will be inserted relative to. Must not be NULL.
 * @param newStmts The vector of SgStatement objects to be inserted into the AST. Must not be empty.
 * @param insertBefore Flag indicating whether to insert the new statements before (true) or after (false) the target statement.
 *
 * @return None
 *
 * @warning This function does not perform any checks on the validity of the input statements or their compatibility with the existing AST structure.
 *
 * @pre The target statement must exist in the AST and the new statements vector must not be empty.
 *
 * @post The new statements are inserted into the AST at the specified position, but no further modifications are made to the AST.
 *
 * @note This function does not handle any potential errors that may occur during the insertion process. It is the caller's responsibility to ensure that the input data is valid and consistent with the expected AST structure.
 *
 * @example This example demonstrates how to use this function:
 *          @code
 *           SgStatement* targetStmt = ...; // obtain a pointer to the target statement in the AST
 *           std::vector<SgStatement*> newStmts; // create a vector of statements to be inserted
 *           newStmts.push_back(...); // add one or more statements to the vector
 *           SageInterface sage;
 *           sage.insertStatementList(targetStmt, newStmts, true); // insert the new statements before the target statement
 *          @endcode
 */
/**
 * @fn void SageInterface::insertStatementBefore(SgStatement* targetStmt, SgStatement* newStmt, bool autoMovePreprocessingInfo)
 *
 * @brief Inserts a statement before another statement in the AST.
 *
 * This function inserts a given statement (newStmt) immediately before
 * another statement (targetStmt) in the Abstract Syntax Tree (AST).
 * It provides an option to automatically move preprocessing information,
 * which is enabled by default.
 *
 * The insertion is performed by calling the insertStatement function,
 * passing the target statement, new statement, and a boolean flag indicating
 * whether the insertion should be done before or after the target statement.
 * In this case, the flag is set to true, meaning the new statement will be inserted
 * before the target statement.
 *
 * @param targetStmt The statement before which the new statement will be inserted.
 *                   Must not be NULL.
 * @param newStmt    The statement to be inserted before the target statement.
 *                  Must not be NULL.
 * @param autoMovePreprocessingInfo Whether preprocessing information should
 *                                   automatically be moved. Defaults to true.
 *
 * @return None (void function)
 *
 * @warning If the target statement is not found in the AST, or if the new statement
 *          cannot be inserted for any reason, this function may throw an exception.
 *
 * @pre The target statement and new statement must both exist in the AST.
 *      The target statement must not be NULL, and the new statement must not be NULL.
 *
 * @post The new statement will have been inserted before the target statement
 *       in the AST, unless an exception was thrown.
 *
 * @note This function calls insertStatement with the before flag set to true.
 *
 * @example This example demonstrates how to use this function:
 *          @code
 *           SgStatement* stmt1 = ...; // some existing statement in the AST
 *           SgStatement* stmt2 = ...; // a new statement to be inserted
 *           SageInterface sage;
 *           sage.insertStatementBefore(stmt1, stmt2);
 *          @endcode
 */
